success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Prepare a release pull request from pending changesets (run in GitHub Actions)

Usage: monochange run release [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>             [default: text] [possible values: text, json, json-min, markdown]
      --no-verify[=<NO_VERIFY>]     [default: true] [possible values: true, false]
      --commit                      Whether to commit the changes
      --create-pr                   Whether to create the PR after the commit
      --write-empty-release-record  Whether to write release records when no packages are released
  -h, --help                        Print help

Release Options:
      --dry-run                  Show what would change without writing files or contacting services
      --diff                     Show unified file diffs for prepared release changes
      --prepared-release <PATH>  Read or write the prepared release artifact at a specific path

Global Options:
  -q, --quiet                     Suppress result, progress, and diagnostic output without changing execution
  -v, --verbose                   Show full result lists and logs, every step timing, and progress notes
      --color <WHEN>              Control when output uses color; `auto` honors NO_COLOR, CLICOLOR, and CLICOLOR_FORCE [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --progress-format <FORMAT>  Control progress output on stderr [possible values: auto, unicode, ascii, json]
      --jq <EXPRESSION>           Filter explicit JSON output; requires `--format json` or `--format json-min`
      --snapshot                  Print a normalized JSON snapshot for this command subtree

Examples:
  monochange run release --dry-run --format text
  monochange run release --dry-run --format json
  monochange run release --dry-run --diff
  monochange run release

Planning reminders:
  - Direct package changes propagate to dependents using defaults.parent_bump or the target's bump_propagation override (including inherit with an optional bump_propagation_max clamp).
  - Group synchronization happens before final output is rendered.
  - Explicit versions on grouped members propagate to the whole group.


